# Build context for the KUL_VBG image.
#
# The image clones KUL_VBG from git at a pinned commit rather than COPYing the
# working tree, so the only thing this context actually needs to carry is
# entrypoint.sh. Everything else is excluded to keep `docker build` from
# uploading the ~180 MB of atlases and test data sitting in the repo.
#
# Note: this file only applies when the build context is this Docker/ directory
# (which is what build.sh does). Building from the repo root would need an
# equivalent .dockerignore there.

*
!entrypoint.sh
!fsl-packages-full.txt
